{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-333105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}+2y,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=0.5,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current value $y?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+2{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side to define $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {{{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.5$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=-\\,y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eaba48976bb1a669129f55ac008d12aa0a9a9db1f28ef56c207abe8db7e6eccb"} {"question" "q-333105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-\\,y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-\\,y-0.5{y}^{2}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-\\,y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3x-{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=0.75,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current value $y?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(3{x}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2})\\cdot 0.75 \\\\  & =2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side to define $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2} \\\\ {{0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.75$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eaba48976bb1a669129f55ac008d12aa0a9a9db1f28ef56c207abe8db7e6eccb"} {"question" "q-333106" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333106" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y+2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.75{y}^{2}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}-y"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.75{y}^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333106" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y-{y}^{3},\\,y(1)=3\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=0.5,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3})\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3} \\\\ {{0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-y}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.5$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-y.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+0.5=1.5.$ Therefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5\\cdot (1.5)^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-3 \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-1.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3 \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eaba48976bb1a669129f55ac008d12aa0a9a9db1f28ef56c207abe8db7e6eccb"} {"question" "q-333119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-3"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}+3"] ["math" "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,y(1.5)=1\n$$\n\nUse the implicit Euler method with one step and Newton's method to approximate $y(2).$ Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n$y(2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=2,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=2-1.5=0.5.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2})\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the equation\n\n$$\n0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.5$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1.5+0.5=2.$ Then, the function $g$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-1-0.5(2)^{2} \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use a root-finding method with starting point $y=1$ to solve $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.$ We'll use Newton's method. \n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}{{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})}\n$$\n\nNote that the derivative of $g$ is\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})=({y}_{\\text{new}})+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton's method iterative scheme is as follows:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{0.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{2}+({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-3}{(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})+1}\n$$\n\nApplying several iterations of Newton's method starting with $y(1.5)=1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}_{\\text{new}})_{1} & =1 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{2} & =1.750000 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{3} & ≈1.647727 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{4} & ≈1.645752\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈1.65,$ rounded to two decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eaba48976bb1a669129f55ac008d12aa0a9a9db1f28ef56c207abe8db7e6eccb"} {"question" "q-333293" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"} {"question" "q-333293" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.65"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066880/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd1ba029accff3df38ed910cd664148c7e3668cd4a9b54468f361c6a3754faeb"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2213 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
